{"_id":"eqwd000000000001","name":"Anashti Sul","type":"deity","img":"systems/eqrmss/assets/Icons/game/abstract-079.svg","system":{"description":"Anashti Sul is the original Prime Healer of Norrath. She was banished to non-existence by the other gods after inadvertently introducing undeath to the world during the Creation Age, a move she later claims was a “gift” to mortals. She is now worshipped as The Undying, an evil-aligned goddess.","alignment":"Evil"}}
{"_id":"eqwd000000000002","name":"Ayonae Ro","type":"deity","img":"systems/eqrmss/assets/Icons/game/abstract-079.svg","system":{"description":"Ayonae Ro is a neutral-aligned demi-goddess in EverQuest, serving as the Maestra of Music and ruler of the Demi-Plane of Music Fanbyte EverQuest+1. She was created by her mother, the demi-goddess Druzzil Ro, specifically to generate music that could soothe the soul Fanbyte EverQuest+1. Druzzil sacrificed a portion of her own realm to give Ayonae her own domain, which she quickly shaped into a lush, tropical island filled with performers and stages.","alignment":"Neutral"}}
{"_id":"eqwd000000000003","name":"Bertoxxulous","type":"deity","img":"systems/eqrmss/assets/Icons/game/abstract-079.svg","system":{"description":"Bertoxxulous is the Plaguebringer, an evil deity in EverQuest and EverQuest II whose followers embrace death, decay, and disease as the ultimate truths of existence.","alignment":"Evil"}}
{"_id":"eqwd000000000004","name":"Brell Serilis","type":"deity","img":"systems/eqrmss/assets/Icons/game/abstract-079.svg","system":{"description":"Brell Serilis was the first to come to Norrath during The Age of Scale, and from his Plane of Underfoot, a dark realm of vast caves and endless tunnels, he quietly created a magical portal to a cavern deep in the belly of Norrath.","alignment":"Neutral"}}
{"_id":"eqwd000000000005","name":"Bristlebane","type":"deity","img":"systems/eqrmss/assets/Icons/game/abstract-079.svg","system":{"description":"Bristlebane is a neutral deity in EverQuest 2, introduced in The Elder Age as part of the second wave of gods. He is the Grand Prankster, ruler of the Plane of Mischief, and creator of the halflings. Known by nicknames such as King of Thieves, Master of Mischief, and Prince of Prank, he embodies fun, mischief, and spontaneity rather than outright malice.","alignment":"Neutral"}}
{"_id":"eqwd000000000006","name":"Cazic-Thule","type":"deity","img":"systems/eqrmss/assets/Icons/game/abstract-079.svg","system":{"description":"Cazic-Thule is the Faceless, Lord of Fear — a dark deity of terror, pain, and domination in EverQuest’s lore.","alignment":"Evil"}}
{"_id":"eqwd000000000007","name":"Coirnav","type":"deity","img":"systems/eqrmss/assets/Icons/game/abstract-079.svg","system":{"description":"Coirnav is the Avatar of Water in EverQuest, a unique divine being created to embody the Triumvirate of Water — the three greater elemental gods of the Plane of Water: Povar (Vapor), E’ci (Ice), and Tarew Marr (Water). Unlike most avatars, which are mere copies of a single deity, Coirnav is a chimera of sea creatures and represents all three deities in unity.","alignment":"Neutral"}}
{"_id":"eqwd000000000008","name":"Drinal","type":"deity","img":"systems/eqrmss/assets/Icons/game/abstract-079.svg","system":{"description":"Drinal is a neutral deity in the EverQuest pantheon, known as The Silver Reaper. He is associated with night, destruction, and death, but is not evil — instead, he represents the necessary end of the cycle of life.","alignment":"Neutral"}}
{"_id":"eqwd000000000009","name":"Druzzil Ro","type":"deity","img":"systems/eqrmss/assets/Icons/game/abstract-079.svg","system":{"description":"Druzzil Ro is the goddess of magic in the EverQuest pantheon, a member of the Ro family of gods and considered Neutral in alignment. She is the Matron of the Art and is often associated with the Plane of Magic, which she shaped into a living canvas reflecting her mood.","alignment":"Neutral"}}
{"_id":"eqwd000000000010","name":"E'ci","type":"deity","img":"systems/eqrmss/assets/Icons/game/abstract-079.svg","system":{"description":"E'ci, known to mortals as the Wintry Guardian, is the second member of the Triumvirate of Water in the EverQuest pantheon. She governs the solid state of water — ice — and embodies its material form and essence. Her domain is the Plane of Water, where she maintains the balance of her element against the other elemental powers.","alignment":"Neutral"}}
{"_id":"eqwd000000000011","name":"Eriak Zek","type":"deity","img":"systems/eqrmss/assets/Icons/game/abstract-079.svg","system":{"description":"Eriak Zek is a sub-deity of Rallos Zek, the Warlord of the ogre nation of Zek, and is considered one of the three brothers of Tallon Zek and Vallon Zek. He is not a full deity in the pantheon but holds a place in the divine hierarchy as a member of the Zek family.","alignment":"Evil"}}
{"_id":"eqwd000000000012","name":"Erollisi Marr","type":"deity","img":"systems/eqrmss/assets/Icons/game/abstract-079.svg","system":{"description":"Erollisi Marr teaches her followers that love conquers all. She, along with her twin brother Mithaniel, created the Barbarians during The Age of Monuments. It is believed that the evolution of Barbarians to Humans was sparked by the divine touch of Erollisi. While love is a beautiful thing, Erollisi's devotees are not so obtuse to believe a Norrath without war is possible. ","alignment":"Good"}}
{"_id":"eqwd000000000013","name":"Fennin Ro","type":"deity","img":"systems/eqrmss/assets/Icons/game/abstract-079.svg","system":{"description":"Fennin Ro is a greater elemental deity in EverQuest, ruling the greater elemental Plane of Fire, also known as Doomfire and the Burning Lands Fanbyte EverQuest+1. His title, The Tyrant of Fire, reflects his fierce devotion to preserving the element of fire, though he is also known for his short temper and wrath when that preservation is threatened ","alignment":"Neutral"}}
{"_id":"eqwd000000000014","name":"Innoruuk","type":"deity","img":"systems/eqrmss/assets/Icons/game/abstract-079.svg","system":{"description":"Almost the entire Dark Elven race sees The Prince of Hate as their true father. They trust in him that hate is the driving force in the universe. Their devotion to hate has led them to believe love is simply a means for the weak-minded fools of the world who are too scared to take what they want. Spite is the only true way to overpower your enemies.","alignment":"Evil"}}
{"_id":"eqwd000000000015","name":"Karana","type":"deity","img":"systems/eqrmss/assets/Icons/game/abstract-079.svg","system":{"description":"Karana is a Greater God in the world of Norrath, ruling the Plane of Storms and serving as the god of rain, storms, thunder, and lightning. He is often called the Rainkeeper or Storm Lord, and is depicted as an elderly man in a deep blue robe, leaning on a withered staff.","alignment":"Good"}}
{"_id":"eqwd000000000016","name":"Kyr'Tok","type":"deity","img":"systems/eqrmss/assets/Icons/game/abstract-079.svg","system":{"description":"Kyr'Tok is a demi‑god from the Plane of Fear (Modinthule), specifically known as The Mangled. While not one of the major deities of Norrath, he is a significant figure in the religious pantheon of the Alliz Tae Ew (lizardmen), who revere him alongside Cazic‑Thule and Alliz Onu.","alignment":"Evil"}}
{"_id":"eqwd000000000017","name":"Luclin","type":"deity","img":"systems/eqrmss/assets/Icons/game/abstract-079.svg","system":{"description":"Luclin is the Mistress of Shadows and the goddess of shadow in the EverQuest universe. She rules the Plane of Shadow and is one of the two moons of Norrath, though she is not currently active on Norrath.","alignment":"Neutral"}}
{"_id":"eqwd000000000018","name":"Master Wu","type":"deity","img":"systems/eqrmss/assets/Icons/game/abstract-079.svg","system":{"description":"Master Wu is a demi-god in the EverQuest universe, known as The Enlightened and the Demi-God of Serenity. He is aligned with Good and is associated with the Plane of Tranquility.","alignment":"Neutral"}}
{"_id":"eqwd000000000019","name":"Mithaniel Marr","type":"deity","img":"systems/eqrmss/assets/Icons/game/abstract-079.svg","system":{"description":"Mithaniel Marr, known as The Truthbringer, is the God of Valor in EverQuest, governing the Plane of Valor Fanbyte EverQuest. He is a pure, untainted embodiment of honor, courage, and selfless sacrifice, and is considered the ultimate paladin — clad in shining silver plate armor and wielding a glowing longsword Fanbyte EverQuest.","alignment":"Good"}}
{"_id":"eqwd000000000020","name":"Morell-Thule","type":"deity","img":"systems/eqrmss/assets/Icons/game/abstract-079.svg","system":{"description":"Morell-Thule is the Lord of Dreams in EverQuest, a deity associated with the Demi-Plane of Dreams, where he governs the rich, vivid textures of sleep visions and the creatures that inhabit them. He is a Good-aligned god, often seen as an outcast son of Cazic-Thule and brother to Terris-Thule, the Goddess of Nightmares.","alignment":"Evil"}}
{"_id":"eqwd000000000021","name":"Povar","type":"deity","img":"systems/eqrmss/assets/Icons/game/abstract-079.svg","system":{"description":"Povar, also known as The Veiled One, is the third member of the Triumvirate of Water in the EverQuest pantheon. This divine entity represents the conscious essence of water in its vaporous state — mist, vapor, and similar forms — and governs a third of the Elemental Plane.","alignment":"Neutral"}}
{"_id":"eqwd000000000022","name":"Prexus","type":"deity","img":"systems/eqrmss/assets/Icons/game/abstract-079.svg","system":{"description":"Prexus is the Ocean Lord in EverQuest, a deity whose worship centers on the power and primordial nature of the world’s oceans.","alignment":"Neutral"}}
{"_id":"eqwd000000000023","name":"Quellious","type":"deity","img":"systems/eqrmss/assets/Icons/game/abstract-079.svg","system":{"description":"Quellious is the Tranquil Goddess of Peace, Patience, and Inner Strength in EverQuest, ruling over the Plane of Tranquility. She is a peaceful deity, but her followers are not strict pacifists — they will defend themselves and loved ones fiercely.","alignment":"Neutral"}}
{"_id":"eqwd000000000024","name":"Rallos Zek","type":"deity","img":"systems/eqrmss/assets/Icons/game/abstract-079.svg","system":{"description":"Rallos Zek is one of the most prominent deities in EverQuest lore, known as The Warlord and aligned with Evil. He is the creator of the most warlike races — Ogres, Giants, Goblins, and Orcs — and embodies the militant ethos of conquest, survival of the strong, and victory above all else.","alignment":"Evil"}}
{"_id":"eqwd000000000025","name":"Rodcet Nife","type":"deity","img":"systems/eqrmss/assets/Icons/game/abstract-079.svg","system":{"description":"Rodcet Nife is the Prime Healer, a benevolent deity devoted to combating disease and death, allied with Karana, Quellious, Erollisi Marr, and Prexus, and opposed solely by Bertoxxulous.","alignment":"Good"}}
{"_id":"eqwd000000000026","name":"Rolfron Zek","type":"deity","img":"systems/eqrmss/assets/Icons/game/abstract-079.svg","system":{"description":"Rolfron Zek is a lesser god in the EverQuest pantheon, often called the Lord of Despair, Hollow God, or Prince of Despair. He is an adopted son of Rallos Zek, the Warlord of the Plane of War, and is considered Neutral Evil in alignment.","alignment":"Evil"}}
{"_id":"eqwd000000000027","name":"Solusek Ro","type":"deity","img":"systems/eqrmss/assets/Icons/game/abstract-079.svg","system":{"description":"Solusek Ro is the god of the sun and flames, ruler of the Plane of Sun, and the Burning Prince to mortals. He is the son of Fennin Ro, the Tyrant of Fire, and is part of the divine Ro clan, which also includes Druzzil and Ayonae.","alignment":"Neutral"}}
{"_id":"eqwd000000000028","name":"Sullon Zek","type":"deity","img":"systems/eqrmss/assets/Icons/game/abstract-079.svg","system":{"description":"Sullon Zek is the Mistress of Rage and goddess of rage in EverQuest, ruling the Plane of Rage and serving as the adopted daughter of Rallos Zek, the god of war. She is also known as the Maiden of Rage and is credited with creating the Bolvirk, a giant-like race native to her plane. Her followers, the Sullonites, are Kerig'Dal who serve her.","alignment":"Evil"}}
{"_id":"eqwd000000000029","name":"Tallon Zek","type":"deity","img":"systems/eqrmss/assets/Icons/game/abstract-079.svg","system":{"description":"Tallon Zek is the Beholder of Battle and the god of strategy in EverQuest, residing on the Plane of War alongside his twin brother Vallon Zek.","alignment":"Neutral"}}
{"_id":"eqwd000000000030","name":"Terris-Thule","type":"deity","img":"systems/eqrmss/assets/Icons/game/abstract-079.svg","system":{"description":"Terris-Thule is the daughter of the Faceless demi-goddess Cazic-Thule and is known for her mastery over the subconscious. She delights in tormenting dreamers, using her plane to trap souls in eternal nightmares. Her twin brother, Morell-Thule, Lord of Dreams, is her foil, representing the realm of dreams.","alignment":"Evil"}}
{"_id":"eqwd000000000031","name":"The Nameless","type":"deity","img":"systems/eqrmss/assets/Icons/game/abstract-079.svg","system":{"description":"In the EverQuest universe, The Nameless is the first known being and the ultimate creator of all existence. It is described as a formless, purposeless power that existed in a vast empty void before the creation of the universe.","alignment":"None"}}
{"_id":"eqwd000000000032","name":"The Rathe","type":"deity","img":"systems/eqrmss/assets/Icons/game/abstract-079.svg","system":{"description":"In EverQuest, the Rathe is the God of Earth and the ruler of the Plane of Earth (also called Vegarlson, the Earthen Badlands). They are not a single deity but a Council of Twelve beings, each with identical grass-green hair, earthen skin, and veins of gold and turquoise. This council is an extension of the plane itself, meaning if one member is destroyed, another will quickly rise to take their place.","alignment":"Neutral"}}
{"_id":"eqwd000000000033","name":"The Tribunal","type":"deity","img":"systems/eqrmss/assets/Icons/game/abstract-079.svg","system":{"description":"The Tribunal is a deified council of six beings who serve as the God of Justice in EverQuest, ruling the Plane of Justice and enforcing impartial, culturally relative justice across Norrath.","alignment":"Neutral"}}
{"_id":"eqwd000000000034","name":"The Triumvirate of Water","type":"deity","img":"systems/eqrmss/assets/Icons/game/abstract-079.svg","system":{"description":"The Triumvirate of Water are three equally powerful deities who jointly govern the elemental Plane of Water, each representing one of its three material states.","alignment":"Neutral"}}
{"_id":"eqwd000000000035","name":"Tholuxe Paells","type":"deity","img":"systems/eqrmss/assets/Icons/game/abstract-079.svg","system":{"description":"Tholuxe Paells is a minor demi‑god in the EverQuest pantheon, best known as the God of Lust. He is considered Chaotic Neutral in alignment and is part of the tier of demi‑gods — divine entities close to mortals in composition but still fully divine in existence.","alignment":"Neutral"}}
{"_id":"eqwd000000000036","name":"Torvonnilous","type":"deity","img":"systems/eqrmss/assets/Icons/game/abstract-079.svg","system":{"description":"Torvonnilous is a demi‑god of greed in the EverQuest pantheon, embodying the essence of material desire and hoarding. He is classified as Chaotic Neutral and is one of the lesser divine beings who still holds a significant role in the lore of Norrath.","alignment":"Neutral"}}
{"_id":"eqwd000000000037","name":"Tunare","type":"deity","img":"systems/eqrmss/assets/Icons/game/abstract-079.svg","system":{"description":"Tunare is the Goddess of Life, Growth, and the Mother of All in EverQuest lore, residing on the Plane of Growth and watching over all living things. She is a Good-aligned deity, often depicted as an older humanoid female in flowing robes and a crown of vines and leaves.","alignment":"Good"}}
{"_id":"eqwd000000000038","name":"Ullkorruuk","type":"deity","img":"systems/eqrmss/assets/Icons/game/abstract-079.svg","system":{"description":"Ullkorruuk is a demi-goddess of betrayal and treachery in the EverQuest universe. She is also known as The Archtraitor or The Lady of Insurrection.","alignment":"Evil"}}
{"_id":"eqwd000000000039","name":"Vallon Zek","type":"deity","img":"systems/eqrmss/assets/Icons/game/abstract-079.svg","system":{"description":"Vallon Zek is the god of tactics and strategy, known as the “Governor of War,” and one of the twin sons of Rallos Zek alongside Tallon Zek.","alignment":"Neutral"}}
{"_id":"eqwd000000000040","name":"Varig Ro","type":"deity","img":"systems/eqrmss/assets/Icons/game/abstract-079.svg","system":{"description":"Varig Ro is a minor deity of Norrath and the god of craftsmanship, particularly renowned as the greatest craftsman in existence everquestlore.fandom.com+1. He is a member of the Ro family of gods, the divine lineage that includes Solusek Ro (god of the sun) and Fennin Ro (god of fire). Varig is the son of Solusek Ro and thus the grandson of Fennin Ro. His exact relationship to other Ro family members like Druzzil and Ayonae is uncertain, but he is part of their divine bloodline.","alignment":"Neutral"}}
{"_id":"eqwd000000000041","name":"Vazaelle","type":"deity","img":"systems/eqrmss/assets/Icons/game/abstract-079.svg","system":{"description":"Vazaelle is the Mad Goddess of Madness, an evil deity whose home plane is the Plane of Madness.","alignment":"Evil"}}
{"_id":"eqwd000000000042","name":"Veeshan","type":"deity","img":"systems/eqrmss/assets/Icons/game/abstract-079.svg","system":{"description":"Veeshan is the Wurmqueen, Goddess of the Sky, and Mother of All Dragons and Dragonkin, ruling the Plane of Sky and marking her claim to Norrath with the Scars of Veeshan.","alignment":"Good"}}
{"_id":"eqwd000000000043","name":"Xegony","type":"deity","img":"systems/eqrmss/assets/Icons/game/abstract-079.svg","system":{"description":"Xegony is the goddess of Air, ruler of the Plane of Air and Eryslai, the Kingdom of Wind, known for her angelic beauty, benevolence, and mysterious nature.","alignment":"Good"}}
{"_id":"eqwd000000000044","name":"Zebuxoruk","type":"deity","img":"systems/eqrmss/assets/Icons/game/abstract-079.svg","system":{"description":"Zebuxoruk is a mysterious and enigmatic figure in the EverQuest pantheon, often described as neither evil nor good, with conflicting legends placing him on opposing sides of morality. He is known by titles such as The Forsaken One and The Disgraced, and is considered an “Ungod” — a being outside the traditional divine hierarchy.","alignment":"Neutral"}}
